  "limitations": [
    "The pair-address mismatch is represented only through the report-stated revert outcome, not as an explicit address inequality, because the salt formula is not reported.",
    "Only the end_rewards_reverts impact is formalized; other listed impacts are out of scope for this plan.",
    "The selected impact is formalized as a progress/liveness obligation: under the stated pair-creation and pairFor conditions, endRewards must complete and terminate rewards accrual.",
    "The address-mismatch root cause and the revert are not encoded as P; they are the reported violation mechanism, not preconditions.",
    "Other listed impacts (end_rewards_reverts, end_rewards_dos, rewards_management_disrupted) are not formalized by this plan.",
    "The exact salt formula and pairFor inputs beyond token0, token1, uniV2InitCodeHash are not specified; the plan encodes only the reported occurrence of pair creation and pairFor computation, not their address equality.",
    "The DoS is represented as the reported revert of endRewards; no concrete revert reason or invalid-address value is bound.",
    "rewards_management_disrupted: No faithful claim generated after bounded retries: distinct P sources reuse identical predicate"
  ]
